{"type":"system","subtype":"commands_changed","commands":[{"name":"_gstack-command","description":"Router for the gstack skill suite. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"agent-roster","description":"Coordinate a user-named roster of models or agents toward a higher-quality consensus without premature convergence. Use when several LLMs should solve, create, review, improve, diagnose, plan, recommend, design, or decide together. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ai-maturity-advancement","description":"Use after an AI maturity/readiness assessment to plan how an organization moves up to the next maturity band. Trigger when someone has a current AI maturity level (L1-L5) or per-dimension scores and asks how to reach the next level, what to fix first, how to cross from one band to the next (e.g. L2 to L3), how to advance specific dimensions (strategy, data, technology, talent, culture, operating model, governance, security, value, agentic autonomy), or wants an AI maturity advancement roadmap, stage plan, or \"path to the next level\". Private consulting playbook; pairs with the ai-readiness-assessment skill. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ai-readiness-assessment","description":"Assess an organization's AI operating readiness with the AI Operating Readiness Framework: 10 dimensions across Foundation, Adoption, and Trust & Scale, each scored 1-5 with governance/security gating and an evidence-calibrated confidence model. Works from company documents, adaptive interactive questions, or a hybrid of both, and returns a maturity band, a recommended agent-autonomy permission, prioritized moves, a path to the next AI maturity level, a readiness debt register, an optional self-contained HTML dashboard, and a personalized outreach email. Use when someone wants to evaluate, score, audit, or benchmark a company's AI readiness, AI maturity, AI adoption, AI governance, or data/tech/talent/culture/agentic readiness — or asks \"are we ready for AI (or AI agents)?\", or wants an AI readiness assessment, scorecard, or roadmap. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"autoplan","description":"Auto-review pipeline — reads the full CEO, design, eng, and DX review skills from disk and runs them sequentially with auto-decisions using 6 decision principles. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"benchmark","description":"Web performance regression detection. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"benchmark-models","description":"Cross-model benchmark for gstack skills. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"bird","description":"X/Twitter CLI for reading, searching, posting, and engagement via cookies. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"browse","description":"Drive a real browser through Aside: open a page, read it, click through a flow, take screenshots, check console errors. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"canary","description":"Post-deploy canary monitoring. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"captain","description":"Run a crew of coding agents from one controller (also /crew): lanes send READY blocks and never merge; the controller merges through trains, keeps the digest, relays approvals, fixes flakes daily. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"careful","description":"Safety guardrails for destructive commands. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"caveman","description":"Ultra-compressed communication mode. Cuts token usage ~75% by dropping filler, articles, and pleasantries while keeping full technical accuracy. Use when user says \"caveman mode\", \"talk like caveman\", \"use caveman\", \"less tokens\", \"be brief\", or invokes /caveman. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"codebase-memory","description":"Use the codebase knowledge graph for structural code queries. Triggers on: explore the codebase, understand the architecture, what functions exist, show me the structure, who calls this function, what does X call, trace the call chain, find callers of, show dependencies, impact analysis, dead code, unused functions, high fan-out, refactor candidates, code quality audit, graph query syntax, Cypher query examples, edge types, how to use search_graph. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"codex","description":"OpenAI Codex CLI wrapper — three modes. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"connect-chrome","description":"Launch GStack Browser — AI-controlled Chromium with the sidebar extension baked in. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"context-restore","description":"Restore working context saved earlier by /context-save. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"context-save","description":"Save working context. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"cso","description":"Security audit: supported static findings; qualified profiles add reproduction and repair candidates. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"design-an-interface","description":"Generate multiple radically different interface designs for a module using parallel sub-agents. Use when user wants to design an API, explore interface options, compare module shapes, or mentions \"design it twice\". (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"design-consultation","description":"Design consultation: understands your product, researches the landscape, proposes a complete design system (aesthetic, typography, color, layout, spacing, motion), and generates font+color preview... (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"design-html","description":"Design finalization: generates production-quality Pretext-native HTML/CSS. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"design-motion","description":"Design motion: animate an approved design into a seamless MP4 and GIF loop. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"design-review","description":"Designer's eye QA: finds visual inconsistency, spacing issues, hierarchy problems, AI slop patterns, and slow interactions — then fixes them. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"design-shotgun","description":"Design shotgun: generate multiple AI design variants, open a comparison board, collect structured feedback, and iterate. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"deslop-shared-libs","description":"Find worthwhile shared-code extractions in recent work. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"devex-review","description":"Live developer experience audit. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"diagnose","description":"Disciplined diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Reproduce → minimise → hypothesise → instrument → fix → regression-test. Use when user says \"diagnose this\" / \"debug this\", reports a bug, says something is broken/throwing/failing, or describes a performance regression. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"diagram","description":"Turn an English description (or mermaid source) into a diagram triplet: the source, an editable .excalidraw file you can open on excalidraw.com, and rendered SVG + PNG. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"document-generate","description":"Generate missing documentation from scratch for a feature, module, or entire project. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"document-release","description":"Release documentation audit. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"edit-article","description":"Edit and improve articles by restructuring sections, improving clarity, and tightening prose. Use when user wants to edit, revise, or improve an article draft. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"eval-plan","description":"Preregister a paid eval (bars, arms, decoys, stop rules), dry-run it at zero cost, then run a three-item priced pilot whose spend table gates approval. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"freeze","description":"Restrict file edits to a specific directory for the session. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"git-guardrails-claude-code","description":"Set up Claude Code hooks to block dangerous git commands (push, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, etc.) before they execute. Use when user wants to prevent destructive git operations, add git safety hooks, or block git push/reset in Claude Code. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"grill-me","description":"Interview the user relentlessly about a plan or design until reaching shared understanding, resolving each branch of the decision tree. Use when user wants to stress-test a plan, get grilled on their design, or mentions \"grill me\". (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"grill-with-docs","description":"Grilling session that challenges your plan against the existing domain model, sharpens terminology, and updates documentation (CONTEXT.md, ADRs) inline as decisions crystallise. Use when user wants to stress-test a plan against their project's language and documented decisions. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gstack","description":"Router for the gstack skill suite. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gstack-upgrade","description":"Upgrade gstack to the latest version. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"guard","description":"Full safety mode: destructive command warnings + directory-scoped edits. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"handoff","description":"Compact the current conversation into a handoff document for another agent to pick up. (user)","argumentHint":"What will the next session be used for?"},{"name":"health","description":"Code quality dashboard. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"hf-cli","description":"Hugging Face Hub CLI (`hf`) for downloading, uploading, and managing models, datasets, spaces, buckets, repos, papers, jobs, and more on the Hugging Face Hub. Use when: handling authentication; managing local cache; managing Hugging Face Buckets; running or scheduling jobs on Hugging Face infrastructure; managing Hugging Face repos; discussions and pull requests; browsing models, datasets and spaces; reading, searching, or browsing academic papers; managing collections; querying datasets; configuring spaces; setting up webhooks; or deploying and managing HF Inference Endpoints. Make sure to use this skill whenever the user mentions 'hf', 'huggingface', 'Hugging Face', 'huggingface-cli', or 'hugging face cli', or wants to do anything related to the Hugging Face ecosystem and to AI and ML in general. Also use for cloud storage needs like training checkpoints, data pipelines, or agent traces. Use even if the user doesn't explicitly ask for a CLI command. Replaces the deprecated `huggingface-cli`. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"humanizer","description":"Remove signs of AI-generated writing from text. Use when editing or reviewing text to make it sound more natural and human-written. Based on Wikipedia's comprehensive \"Signs of AI writing\" guide. Detects and fixes patterns including: inflated symbolism, promotional language, superficial -ing analyses, vague attributions, em dash overuse, rule of three, AI vocabulary words, negative parallelisms, and excessive conjunctive phrases. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"implement","description":"Execute an existing software implementation Plan as a dependency-aware campaign of isolated, parallel pull requests. Use when the user provides or attaches a Plan and chooses Builder models, one final Reviewer model, and optionally the Best-of-N width. Each Plan item becomes its own tested PR; independent items run concurrently by default; CI failures, review findings, and merge conflicts are repaired automatically before green-gated merge or handoff. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"improve-codebase-architecture","description":"Find deepening opportunities in a codebase, informed by the domain language in CONTEXT.md and the decisions in docs/adr/. Use when the user wants to improve architecture, find refactoring opportunities, consolidate tightly-coupled modules, or make a codebase more testable and AI-navigable. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"investigate","description":"Systematic debugging with root cause investigation. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ios-clean","description":"Remove the DebugBridge SPM package and all #if DEBUG wiring from an iOS app. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ios-design-review","description":"Visual design audit for iOS apps on real hardware. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ios-fix","description":"Autonomous iOS bug fixer. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ios-qa","description":"Live-device iOS QA for SwiftUI apps. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ios-sync","description":"Regenerate the iOS debug bridge against the latest upstream gstack templates. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"land-and-deploy","description":"Land and deploy workflow. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"landing-report","description":"Read-only queue dashboard for workspace-aware ship. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"laya-gate","description":"Local Laya-MLX typed gate: allow/deny tool actions and route quick vs full Hermes turns in milliseconds. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"learn","description":"Manage project learnings. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"make-pdf","description":"Turn any markdown file into a publication-quality PDF. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"migrate-to-shoehorn","description":"Migrate test files from `as` type assertions to @total-typescript/shoehorn. Use when user mentions shoehorn, wants to replace `as` in tests, or needs partial test data. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"modernize","description":"Bring an aging pull request onto its current base and decide whether it should still exist: MODERNIZE, REWORK or CLOSE, with range-diff proof before any push. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"no-ai-slop","description":"Edit drafts into sharper, more human writing while preserving the writer's personal voice, or detect AI-slop patterns without rewriting. Use when the user wants a draft clearer, more direct, more opinionated, or less AI-sounding, or asks whether writing reads as AI. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"obsidian-vault","description":"Search, create, and manage notes in the Obsidian vault with wikilinks and index notes. Use when user wants to find, create, or organize notes in Obsidian. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"office-hours","description":"YC Office Hours — two modes. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"open-gstack-browser","description":"Launch GStack Browser — AI-controlled Chromium with the sidebar extension baked in. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"opinions-agent","description":"Connect to Opinions, build the user's source library, import public X observations with approved access, and write a personal briefing from cited evidence. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"pair-agent","description":"Pair a remote AI agent with your browser. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"plan-ceo-review","description":"CEO/founder-mode plan review. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"plan-design-review","description":"Designer's eye plan review — interactive, like CEO and Eng review. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"plan-devex-review","description":"Interactive developer experience plan review. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"plan-eng-review","description":"Eng manager-mode plan review. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"plan-tune","description":"Self-tuning question sensitivity + developer psychographic for gstack (v1: observational). (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"planning-with-files","description":"Implements Manus-style file-based planning for complex tasks. Creates task_plan.md, findings.md, and progress.md. Use when starting complex multi-step tasks, research projects, or any task requiring &gt;5 tool calls. Now with automatic session recovery after /clear. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"prototype","description":"Build a throwaway prototype to flesh out a design before committing to it. Routes between two branches — a runnable terminal app for state/business-logic questions, or several radically different UI variations toggleable from one route. Use when the user wants to prototype, sanity-check a data model or state machine, mock up a UI, explore design options, or says \"prototype this\", \"let me play with it\", \"try a few designs\". (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"qa","description":"Test the site, API or CLI and fix the bugs it finds. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"qa-only","description":"Report browser/API/CLI/job/worker/webhook bugs. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"remove-ai-slop","description":"Edit, audit, or draft prose that should sound specific and human without changing its facts or flattening the writer's voice. Use when the user asks to remove AI tells, humanize writing, de-slop a draft, preserve a personal voice, check prose for formulaic patterns, or clean prose in a file or docs tree. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"request-refactor-plan","description":"Create a detailed refactor plan with tiny commits via user interview, then file it as a GitHub issue. Use when user wants to plan a refactor, create a refactoring RFC, or break a refactor into safe incremental steps. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"researchos","description":"Use ResearchOS Research CI and Conductor from Claude Code for verification-gated research loops. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"retro","description":"Weekly engineering retrospective. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"review","description":"Review this PR's diff. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"scaffold-exercises","description":"Create exercise directory structures with sections, problems, solutions, and explainers that pass linting. Use when user wants to scaffold exercises, create exercise stubs, or set up a new course section. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"scrape","description":"Pull data from a web page through the Aside browser — your real, already signed-in sessions. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"setup-browser-cookies","description":"Import cookies from your real Chromium browser into the headless browse session. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"setup-deploy","description":"Configure deployment settings for /land-and-deploy. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"setup-gbrain","description":"Set up gbrain for this coding agent: install the CLI, initialize a local PGLite or Supabase brain, register MCP, capture per-remote trust policy. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"setup-matt-pocock-skills","description":"Sets up an `## Agent skills` block in AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md and `docs/agents/` so the engineering skills know this repo's issue tracker (GitHub or local markdown), triage label vocabulary, and domain doc layout. Run before first use of `to-issues`, `to-prd`, `triage`, `diagnose`, `tdd`, `improve-codebase-architecture`, or `zoom-out` — or if those skills appear to be missing context about the issue tracker, triage labels, or domain docs. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"setup-pre-commit","description":"Set up Husky pre-commit hooks with lint-staged (Prettier), type checking, and tests in the current repo. Use when user wants to add pre-commit hooks, set up Husky, configure lint-staged, or add commit-time formatting/typechecking/testing. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ship","description":"Ship it: merge the base, run tests, review the diff, bump VERSION and CHANGELOG, push and create a PR. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"skillify","description":"Codify the most recent successful /scrape flow into a permanent browser-skill on disk. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solve","description":"Attack a hard open problem with a multi-model adversarial research lab that runs several research directions in parallel. Opus 4.8 is the PI/conductor: it pins the exact target, spawns parallel SUB-TEAMS (one per distinct research direction), each dispatching DISTINCT attack angles to a diverse worker panel (Codex GPT-5.5 xhigh, DeepSeek-V4-Pro, MiniMax-M3, Kimi-k2.7-code), adversarially cross-verifies every claim with a different model, ground-truths finite claims with exact computation, resolves every citation against primary source, folds in external human/referee feedback (which the PI adjudicates — it is the final reviewer and sole decider of the next round), and tracks an analytically-defined progress metric (proof-DAG coverage % or a distance-to-goal coordinate when the problem is closeable; calibrated success odds when it is open) round by round under a kill criterion until rigorous consensus — survival of refutation, not majority vote. Use whenever the user wants to seriously attack a research problem, conjecture, open question, prize/bounty, hard theorem, or derivation — especially when they type /solve or mention a \"research lab\", \"multi-agent\", \"sub-teams\", \"prove or disprove\", \"attack this\", \"how much progress\", or want robust, independently verified results with a real progress measure instead of a confident guess. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"spec","description":"Turn vague intent into a precise, executable spec in five phases. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"sync-gbrain","description":"Keep gbrain current with this repo's code and refresh agent search guidance in CLAUDE.md. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"tdd","description":"Test-driven development with red-green-refactor loop. Use when user wants to build features or fix bugs using TDD, mentions \"red-green-refactor\", wants integration tests, or asks for test-first development. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"teach","description":"Teach the user a new skill or concept, within this workspace. (user)","argumentHint":"What would you like to learn about?"},{"name":"test-audit","description":"Find low-value or duplicate tests and the test-only code they keep alive. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"to-issues","description":"Break a plan, spec, or PRD into independently-grabbable issues on the project issue tracker using tracer-bullet vertical slices. Use when user wants to convert a plan into issues, create implementation tickets, or break down work into issues. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"to-prd","description":"Turn the current conversation context into a PRD and publish it to the project issue tracker. Use when user wants to create a PRD from the current context. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"triage","description":"Triage issues through a state machine driven by triage roles. Use when user wants to create an issue, triage issues, review incoming bugs or feature requests, prepare issues for an AFK agent, or manage issue workflow. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ubicloud","description":"Run a heavy suite, build or eval on an ephemeral 16-vCPU Ubicloud VM: TTL-named VMs, a reaper, quota preflight and a hang watchdog. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ubiquitous-language","description":"Extract a DDD-style ubiquitous language glossary from the current conversation, flagging ambiguities and proposing canonical terms. Saves to UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md. Use when user wants to define domain terms, build a glossary, harden terminology, create a ubiquitous language, or mentions \"domain model\" or \"DDD\". (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"unfreeze","description":"Clear the freeze boundary set by /freeze, allowing edits to all directories again. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"verify","description":"Build loop while coding: run the repo's checks and the tests /ship would pick, fix, repeat until green. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"work-board","description":"Personal work board: the user's live claude.ai page that holds open decision cards and every running job. Use this skill even when the user never says \"board\". It covers three intents: - The user owes a decision. You need their call on a choice (drop a version, pick a time, approve a plan), or they say \"ask async\", \"don't block on me\", \"keep going\" or \"park it\". Post a decision card first, then continue other work. - The user asks about their own queue: what waits on them, what is blocked on their answer, what needs them, what is in flight. This also covers a reply that is only an option number, such as \"2\". - A job changes state. A PR opens, merges or fails. CI, a review or a deploy starts or ends. A long task stalls. This also covers the user reporting such news, saying the board is stale, or a \"board pickup\" run. Do not use it to build kanban apps or dashboards, or for advice on Jira, Trello or GitHub project boards. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"write-a-skill","description":"Create new agent skills with proper structure, progressive disclosure, and bundled resources. Use when user wants to create, write, or build a new skill. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"write-skill","description":"Write a new agent skill or improve one without bloat: the edit ladder, levels, drift and size checks, full diets. (gstack) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"writing-beats","description":"Shape an article as a journey of beats, choose-your-own-adventure style. The user picks a starting beat from the raw material, you write only that beat, then offer options for where to pivot next, beat by beat, until the article reaches a natural end. Use when the user has raw material and wants to assemble it as a narrative rather than an argument. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"writing-fragments","description":"Grilling session that mines the user for fragments — heterogeneous nuggets of writing (claims, vignettes, sharp sentences, half-thoughts) — and appends them to a single document as raw material for a future article. Use when the user wants to develop ideas before imposing structure, or mentions \"fragments\", \"ideate\", or \"raw material\" for writing. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"writing-shape","description":"Take a markdown file of raw material and shape it into an article through a conversational session — drafting candidate openings, growing the piece paragraph by paragraph, arguing about format (lists, tables, callouts, quotes) at each step. Use when the user has a pile of notes, fragments, or a rough draft and wants help turning it into something publishable. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"zoom-out","description":"Tell the agent to zoom out and give broader context or a higher-level perspective. Use when you're unfamiliar with a section of code or need to understand how it fits into the bigger picture. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:add-phase","description":"Add research phase to end of current milestone in roadmap (user)","argumentHint":"<description>"},{"name":"gpd:add-todo","description":"Capture idea or task as todo from current research conversation context (user)","argumentHint":"[optional description]"},{"name":"gpd:arxiv-submission","description":"Prepare a GPD-owned manuscript for arXiv submission with validation and packaging (user)","argumentHint":"[manuscript root or .tex entrypoint]"},{"name":"gpd:audit-milestone","description":"Audit research milestone completion against original research goals (user)","argumentHint":"[version]"},{"name":"gpd:autonomous","description":"Run all remaining phases autonomously — discuss→plan→execute→verify per phase (user)","argumentHint":"[--from N]"},{"name":"gpd:branch-hypothesis","description":"Create a hypothesis branch for parallel investigation of an alternative approach (user)","argumentHint":"<description>"},{"name":"gpd:check-todos","description":"List pending research todos and select one to work on (user)","argumentHint":"[area filter]"},{"name":"gpd:compact-state","description":"Archive historical entries from STATE.md to keep it under the 150-line target (user)","argumentHint":"[--force]"},{"name":"gpd:compare-branches","description":"Compare results across hypothesis branches side-by-side (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:compare-experiment","description":"Systematically compare theoretical predictions with experimental or observational data (user)","argumentHint":"[prediction, dataset, phase, or comparison target]"},{"name":"gpd:compare-results","description":"Compare internal results, baselines, or methods and emit decisive verdicts (user)","argumentHint":"[comparison target or source-a vs source-b]"},{"name":"gpd:complete-milestone","description":"Archive completed research milestone and prepare for next phase of investigation (user)","argumentHint":"<version>"},{"name":"gpd:debug","description":"Systematic debugging of physics calculations with persistent state across context resets (user)","argumentHint":"[issue description]"},{"name":"gpd:decisions","description":"Display and search the cumulative decision log (user)","argumentHint":"[phase number or keyword]"},{"name":"gpd:derive-equation","description":"Perform a rigorous physics derivation with systematic verification at each step (user)","argumentHint":"[equation or topic to derive]"},{"name":"gpd:digest-knowledge","description":"Create or update a draft knowledge document in the current workspace from a topic, source file, arXiv ID, or canonical knowledge path (user)","argumentHint":"[topic | source file | arXiv ID | current-workspace GPD/knowledge/K-*.md]"},{"name":"gpd:dimensional-analysis","description":"Systematic dimensional analysis audit on all equations in a derivation or phase (user)","argumentHint":"[phase number or file path]"},{"name":"gpd:discover","description":"Run discovery phase to investigate methods, literature, and approaches before planning (user)","argumentHint":"[phase or topic] [--depth quick|medium|deep]"},{"name":"gpd:discuss-phase","description":"Gather phase context through adaptive questioning before planning (user)","argumentHint":"<phase> [--auto|--compact]"},{"name":"gpd:error-patterns","description":"View accumulated physics error patterns for this project (user)","argumentHint":"[category]"},{"name":"gpd:error-propagation","description":"Track how uncertainties propagate through multi-step calculations across phases (user)","argumentHint":"[--target quantity] [--phase-range start:end]"},{"name":"gpd:execute-phase","description":"Execute all plans in a phase with wave-based parallelization (user)","argumentHint":"<phase-number> [--gaps-only]"},{"name":"gpd:explain","description":"Explain a physics concept rigorously in the context of the active project or a standalone question with an explicit topic (user)","argumentHint":"[concept, result, method, notation, or paper]"},{"name":"gpd:export","description":"Export research results to HTML, LaTeX, or ZIP package (user)","argumentHint":"[--format html|latex|zip|all] [--commit]"},{"name":"gpd:export-logs","description":"Export session logs and traces to files for external review or archival (user)","argumentHint":"[--format jsonl|json|markdown] [--session <id>] [--last N] [--command <label>] [--phase <phase>] [--category <name>] [--no-traces] [--output-dir <path>]"},{"name":"gpd:graph","description":"Visualize dependency graph across phases and identify gaps (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:health","description":"Run project health checks and optionally auto-fix issues (user)","argumentHint":"[--fix]"},{"name":"gpd:help","description":"Show available GPD commands and usage guide (user)","argumentHint":"[--all | --command <name>]"},{"name":"gpd:insert-phase","description":"Insert urgent research work as decimal phase (e.g., 72.1) between existing phases (user)","argumentHint":"<after-phase> \"<description>\""},{"name":"gpd:limiting-cases","description":"Systematically identify and verify all relevant limiting cases for a result or phase (user)","argumentHint":"[phase number or file path]"},{"name":"gpd:list-phase-assumptions","description":"Surface the AI's assumptions about a phase approach before planning (user)","argumentHint":"<phase-number>"},{"name":"gpd:literature-review","description":"Structured literature review for a physics research topic with citation network analysis and open question identification (user)","argumentHint":"[topic or research question]"},{"name":"gpd:map-research","description":"Map existing research project — theoretical framework, computations, conventions, and open questions (user)","argumentHint":"[optional: specific area to map, e.g., 'hamiltonian' or 'numerics' or 'perturbation-theory']"},{"name":"gpd:merge-phases","description":"Merge results from one phase into another (user)","argumentHint":"<source-phase> <target-phase>"},{"name":"gpd:new-milestone","description":"Start a new research milestone cycle — staged init, requirements, and roadmap (user)","argumentHint":"[milestone name, e.g., 'v1.1 Finite-Temperature Extension']"},{"name":"gpd:new-project","description":"Initialize a new physics research project with deep context gathering and PROJECT.md (user)","argumentHint":"[--auto] [--minimal [@file.md]]"},{"name":"gpd:numerical-convergence","description":"Systematic convergence testing for numerical physics computations (user)","argumentHint":"[phase number or file path]"},{"name":"gpd:parameter-sweep","description":"Systematic parameter sweep with parallel execution and result aggregation (user)","argumentHint":"[phase | computation anchor] [--param name --range start:end:steps] [--adaptive] [--log]"},{"name":"gpd:pause-work","description":"Create continuation handoff when pausing research mid-phase (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:peer-review","description":"Conduct a staged six-pass peer review of a manuscript and supporting research artifacts from the current GPD project or an explicit external artifact (user)","argumentHint":"[paper directory or manuscript/artifact path]"},{"name":"gpd:plan-milestone-gaps","description":"Create phases to close all gaps identified by research milestone audit (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:plan-phase","description":"Create detailed execution plan for a phase (PLAN.md) with verification loop (user)","argumentHint":"[phase] [--research] [--skip-research] [--gaps] [--skip-verify] [--light] [--inline-discuss]"},{"name":"gpd:progress","description":"Check research progress, show context, and route to next action (execute or plan) (user)","argumentHint":"[--brief | --full | --reconcile]"},{"name":"gpd:quick","description":"Execute a quick research task with GPD guarantees (atomic commits, state tracking) but skip optional agents (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:reapply-patches","description":"Reapply local modifications after a GPD update (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:record-backtrack","description":"Record a backtrack event (what went wrong, what got reverted) to the backtracks ledger (user)","argumentHint":"[--reverted-commit=<sha>] [--trigger=<text>] [--phase=<NN-slug>] [description]"},{"name":"gpd:record-insight","description":"Record a project-specific learning or pattern to the insights ledger (user)","argumentHint":"[optional description]"},{"name":"gpd:regression-check","description":"Scan completed phase summaries and verifications for convention conflicts and verification-state regressions (user)","argumentHint":"[phase] [--quick]"},{"name":"gpd:remove-phase","description":"Remove a future research phase from roadmap and renumber subsequent phases (user)","argumentHint":"<phase-number>"},{"name":"gpd:research-phase","description":"Research how to tackle a phase (standalone - usually use /gpd:plan-phase instead) (user)","argumentHint":"<phase-number>"},{"name":"gpd:respond-to-referees","description":"Structure a point-by-point response to referee reports for an explicit manuscript target or the current GPD manuscript (user)","argumentHint":"[--manuscript PATH] (--report PATH [--report PATH...] | paste)"},{"name":"gpd:resume-work","description":"Resume research from previous session with full context restoration (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:review-knowledge","description":"Review a current-workspace knowledge document for approval, changes, or promotion gating (user)","argumentHint":"[current-workspace GPD/knowledge/{knowledge_id}.md | canonical K-* knowledge_id]"},{"name":"gpd:revise-phase","description":"Supersede a completed phase and create a replacement for iterative revision (user)","argumentHint":"<phase-number> <reason for revision>"},{"name":"gpd:route","description":"Decide whether a scope change is a new phase, a revision, a new milestone, or a milestone completion (user)","argumentHint":"[--frozen=yes|no] [--change=extend|revise] [--layer=new|change]"},{"name":"gpd:sensitivity-analysis","description":"Systematic sensitivity analysis -- which parameters matter most and how uncertainties propagate (user)","argumentHint":"[--target quantity] [--params p1,p2,...] [--method analytical|numerical]"},{"name":"gpd:set-profile","description":"Switch research profile for GPD agents (deep-theory/numerical/exploratory/review/paper-writing) (user)","argumentHint":"<profile>"},{"name":"gpd:set-tier-models","description":"Configure concrete tier-1/tier-2/tier-3 model IDs for the active runtime (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:settings","description":"Configure autonomy, unattended execution budgets, runtime permission sync, workflow preset bundles, model-cost posture, runtime-specific tier model overrides, review cadence, and git preferences (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:show-phase","description":"Inspect a single phase's artifacts, status, and results (user)","argumentHint":"<phase-number>"},{"name":"gpd:slides","description":"Create presentation slides from a GPD project or the current folder (user)","argumentHint":"[topic, talk title, audience, or source path]"},{"name":"gpd:start","description":"Choose the right first GPD action for this folder and route into the real workflow (user)","argumentHint":"[optional short goal]"},{"name":"gpd:suggest-next","description":"Suggest the most impactful next action based on current project state (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:sync-state","description":"Reconcile diverged STATE.md and state.json after manual edits or corruption (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:tangent","description":"Choose how to handle a possible side investigation without silently widening scope (user)","argumentHint":"[optional description]"},{"name":"gpd:tour","description":"Show a guided beginner walkthrough of the core GPD commands without taking action (user)","argumentHint":"[optional short goal]"},{"name":"gpd:undo","description":"Rollback last GPD operation with safety checkpoint (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:update","description":"Update GPD to latest version with changelog display (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"gpd:validate-conventions","description":"Validate convention consistency across all phases (user)","argumentHint":"[phase number to limit scope, or empty for all]"},{"name":"gpd:verify-work","description":"Verify research results through physics consistency checks (user)","argumentHint":"[phase] [--dimensional] [--limits] [--convergence] [--regression] [--all]"},{"name":"gpd:write-paper","description":"Structure and write a physics paper from project research results or a bounded external-authoring intake (user)","argumentHint":"[--intake path/to/write-paper-authoring-input.json]"},{"name":"solidity-auditor","description":"Security audit of Solidity code while you develop. Trigger on \"audit\", \"check this contract\", \"review for security\". Modes - default (full repo), DEEP (+ adversarial reasoning), or a specific filename. (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:assets:docs:README","description":"Project Docs (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:assets:findings:README","description":"Findings (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:agents:adversarial-reasoning-agent","description":"Adversarial Reasoning Agent Instructions (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:agents:vector-scan-agent","description":"Vector Scan Agent Instructions (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:attack-vectors:attack-vectors-1","description":"Attack Vectors Reference (1/4) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:attack-vectors:attack-vectors-2","description":"Attack Vectors Reference (2/4) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:attack-vectors:attack-vectors-3","description":"Attack Vectors Reference (3/4) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:attack-vectors:attack-vectors-4","description":"Attack Vectors Reference (4/4) (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:judging","description":"Finding Validation (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"solidity-auditor:references:report-formatting","description":"Report Formatting (user)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z","description":"Zero — orient, enter entities, and route work. (user)","argumentHint":"[<command>] [<args>]"},{"name":"deep-research","description":"Deep research harness — fan-out web searches, fetch sources, adversarially verify claims, synthesize a cited report. (dynamic workflow)","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"ralph-loop:cancel-ralph","description":"(ralph-loop) Cancel active Ralph Loop","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ralph-loop:help","description":"(ralph-loop) Explain Ralph Loop plugin and available commands","argumentHint":""},{"name":"ralph-loop:ralph-loop","description":"(ralph-loop) Start Ralph Loop in current session","argumentHint":"PROMPT [--max-iterations N] [--completion-promise TEXT]"},{"name":"superpowers:brainstorming","description":"(superpowers) You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, modifying behavior, or planning anything new, in software or out of it (a talk, a business, a renovation).","argumentHint":"","aliases":["brainstorming"]},{"name":"superpowers:diagnosing-superpowers","description":"(superpowers) Use when a superpowers session went wrong and your human partner wants to know why — repeated work, ignored plans, stumbles, poor results, a skill that didn't fire, \"it took too long\", \"why is it so expensive\", \"what is it doing\" — or wants to build a bug report for the superpowers maintainers, for the current session or a past one identified by id or path, on any harness.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["diagnosing-superpowers"]},{"name":"superpowers:dispatching-parallel-agents","description":"(superpowers) Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies","argumentHint":"","aliases":["dispatching-parallel-agents"]},{"name":"superpowers:executing-plans","description":"(superpowers) Use when executing an implementation plan in the current session as the implementer yourself — your human partner chose inline execution, or no subagent tool is available","argumentHint":"","aliases":["executing-plans"]},{"name":"superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch","description":"(superpowers) Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work","argumentHint":"","aliases":["finishing-a-development-branch"]},{"name":"superpowers:receiving-code-review","description":"(superpowers) Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation","argumentHint":"","aliases":["receiving-code-review"]},{"name":"superpowers:requesting-code-review","description":"(superpowers) Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements","argumentHint":"","aliases":["requesting-code-review"]},{"name":"superpowers:subagent-driven-development","description":"(superpowers) Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session","argumentHint":"","aliases":["subagent-driven-development"]},{"name":"superpowers:systematic-debugging","description":"(superpowers) Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","argumentHint":"","aliases":["systematic-debugging"]},{"name":"superpowers:test-driven-development","description":"(superpowers) Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","argumentHint":"","aliases":["test-driven-development"]},{"name":"superpowers:using-git-worktrees","description":"(superpowers) Use when starting feature work that needs isolation from current workspace or before executing implementation plans - ensures an isolated workspace exists via native tools or git worktree fallback","argumentHint":"","aliases":["using-git-worktrees"]},{"name":"superpowers:using-superpowers","description":"(superpowers) Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring skill invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions","argumentHint":"","aliases":["using-superpowers"]},{"name":"superpowers:verification-before-completion","description":"(superpowers) Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always","argumentHint":"","aliases":["verification-before-completion"]},{"name":"superpowers:writing-plans","description":"(superpowers) Use when you have a spec or requirements for a multi-step task, before touching code","argumentHint":"","aliases":["writing-plans"]},{"name":"superpowers:writing-skills","description":"(superpowers) Use when creating new skills, editing existing skills, or verifying skills work before deployment","argumentHint":"","aliases":["writing-skills"]},{"name":"engineering:architecture","description":"(engineering) Create or evaluate an architecture decision record (ADR). Use when choosing between technologies (e.g., Kafka vs SQS), documenting a design decision with trade-offs and consequences, reviewing a system design proposal, or designing a new component from requirements and constraints.","argumentHint":"<decision or system to design>","aliases":["architecture"]},{"name":"engineering:code-review","description":"(engineering) Review code changes for security, performance, and correctness. Trigger with a PR URL or diff, \"review this before I merge\", \"is this code safe?\", or when checking a change for N+1 queries, injection risks, missing edge cases, or error handling gaps.","argumentHint":"<PR URL, diff, or file path>"},{"name":"engineering:debug","description":"(engineering) Structured debugging session — reproduce, isolate, diagnose, and fix. Trigger with an error message or stack trace, \"this works in staging but not prod\", \"something broke after the deploy\", or when behavior diverges from expected and the cause isn't obvious.","argumentHint":"<error message or problem description>"},{"name":"engineering:deploy-checklist","description":"(engineering) Pre-deployment verification checklist. Use when about to ship a release, deploying a change with database migrations or feature flags, verifying CI status and approvals before going to production, or documenting rollback triggers ahead of time.","argumentHint":"[service or release name]","aliases":["deploy-checklist"]},{"name":"engineering:documentation","description":"(engineering) Write and maintain technical documentation. Trigger with \"write docs for\", \"document this\", \"create a README\", \"write a runbook\", \"onboarding guide\", or when the user needs help with any form of technical writing — API docs, architecture docs, or operational runbooks.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["documentation"]},{"name":"engineering:incident-response","description":"(engineering) Run an incident response workflow — triage, communicate, and write postmortem. Trigger with \"we have an incident\", \"production is down\", an alert that needs severity assessment, a status update mid-incident, or when writing a blameless postmortem after resolution.","argumentHint":"<incident description or alert>","aliases":["incident-response"]},{"name":"engineering:standup","description":"(engineering) Generate a standup update from recent activity. Use when preparing for daily standup, summarizing yesterday's commits and PRs and ticket moves, formatting work into yesterday/today/blockers, or structuring a few rough notes into a shareable update.","argumentHint":"[yesterday | today | blockers]","aliases":["standup"]},{"name":"engineering:system-design","description":"(engineering) Design systems, services, and architectures. Trigger with \"design a system for\", \"how should we architect\", \"system design for\", \"what's the right architecture for\", or when the user needs help with API design, data modeling, or service boundaries.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["system-design"]},{"name":"engineering:tech-debt","description":"(engineering) Identify, categorize, and prioritize technical debt. Trigger with \"tech debt\", \"technical debt audit\", \"what should we refactor\", \"code health\", or when the user asks about code quality, refactoring priorities, or maintenance backlog.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["tech-debt"]},{"name":"engineering:testing-strategy","description":"(engineering) Design test strategies and test plans. Trigger with \"how should we test\", \"test strategy for\", \"write tests for\", \"test plan\", \"what tests do we need\", or when the user needs help with testing approaches, coverage, or test architecture.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["testing-strategy"]},{"name":"cowork-plugin-management:cowork-plugin-customizer","description":"(cowork-plugin-management) Customize a Claude Code plugin for a specific organization's tools and workflows. Use when: customize plugin, set up plugin, configure plugin, tailor plugin, adjust plugin settings, customize plugin connectors, customize plugin skill, tweak plugin, modify plugin configuration.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["cowork-plugin-customizer"]},{"name":"cowork-plugin-management:create-cowork-plugin","description":"(cowork-plugin-management) Guide users through creating a new plugin from scratch in a cowork session. Use when users want to create a plugin, build a plugin, make a new plugin, develop a plugin, scaffold a plugin, start a plugin from scratch, or design a plugin. This skill requires Cowork mode with access to the outputs directory for delivering the final .plugin file.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["create-cowork-plugin"]},{"name":"design:accessibility-review","description":"(design) Run a WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility audit on a design or page. Trigger with \"audit accessibility\", \"check a11y\", \"is this accessible?\", or when reviewing a design for color contrast, keyboard navigation, touch target size, or screen reader behavior before handoff.","argumentHint":"<Figma URL, URL, or description>","aliases":["accessibility-review"]},{"name":"design:design-critique","description":"(design) Get structured design feedback on usability, hierarchy, and consistency. Trigger with \"review this design\", \"critique this mockup\", \"what do you think of this screen?\", or when sharing a Figma link or screenshot for feedback at any stage from exploration to final polish.","argumentHint":"<Figma URL, screenshot, or description>","aliases":["design-critique"]},{"name":"design:design-handoff","description":"(design) Generate developer handoff specs from a design. Use when a design is ready for engineering and needs a spec sheet covering layout, design tokens, component props, interaction states, responsive breakpoints, edge cases, and animation details.","argumentHint":"<Figma URL or design description>","aliases":["design-handoff"]},{"name":"design:design-system","description":"(design) Audit, document, or extend your design system. Use when checking for naming inconsistencies or hardcoded values across components, writing documentation for a component's variants, states, and accessibility notes, or designing a new pattern that fits the existing system.","argumentHint":"[audit | document | extend] <component or system>","aliases":["design-system"]},{"name":"design:research-synthesis","description":"(design) Synthesize user research into themes, insights, and recommendations. Use when you have interview transcripts, survey results, usability test notes, support tickets, or NPS responses that need to be distilled into patterns, user segments, and prioritized next steps.","argumentHint":"<research data, transcripts, or survey results>","aliases":["research-synthesis"]},{"name":"design:user-research","description":"(design) Plan, conduct, and synthesize user research. Trigger with \"user research plan\", \"interview guide\", \"usability test\", \"survey design\", \"research questions\", or when the user needs help with any aspect of understanding their users through research.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["user-research"]},{"name":"design:ux-copy","description":"(design) Write or review UX copy — microcopy, error messages, empty states, CTAs. Trigger with \"write copy for\", \"what should this button say?\", \"review this error message\", or when naming a CTA, wording a confirmation dialog, filling an empty state, or writing onboarding text.","argumentHint":"<context or copy to review>","aliases":["ux-copy"]},{"name":"design","description":"Make a new Design artifact from a brief","argumentHint":"[what to design]","builtin":true},{"name":"slides","description":"Make a new Slides deck artifact from a brief","argumentHint":"[what the deck is about]","builtin":true},{"name":"design-sync","description":"Push a React design system to claude.ai/design. This runs a converter that bundles the real component code (from Storybook or a bare package) and uploads it. Use when the user runs /design-sync or says \"sync my design system to Claude Design\".","argumentHint":"[<project hint, e.g. \"Acme DS\">]","builtin":true},{"name":"dataviz","description":"Use this skill whenever you are about to create ANY chart, graph, plot, dashboard, or data visualization, in ANY output medium — an HTML or React artifact, inline SVG, plotting code in any library (matplotlib, plotly, d3, Recharts, …), an image/PNG you will render and upload, or a chart shared into Slack. Read it BEFORE writing the first line of chart code, choosing chart colors, building a stat tile / meter / KPI row, or laying out a dashboard. When the destination is a first-party document connector (host-designated, never self-described) that renders live charts, hand it the rows (inline, or as an uploaded data file the chart cites) rather than a rendered PNG/SVG — a picture of a chart loses hover, data inspection and per-value comments. Produces visualizations that read as one system — elegant, accessible, consistent in light and dark — using a brand-neutral placeholder palette you swap for your own. Teaches a design-system-agnostic method: a form heuristic, a color formula with a runnable validator, mark specs, and interaction rules. A validated default palette is documented in `references/palette.md` — swap that file's values for your brand's. Triggers on: \"chart\", \"graph\", \"plot\", \"data viz\", \"visualization\", \"dashboard\", \"analytics\", \"visualize data\", \"categorical colors\", \"sequential / diverging palette\", \"stat tile\", \"sparkline\", \"heatmap\", \"legend\", \"axis\", \"tooltip\", \"chart colors\", \"color by series\".","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"artifact-diagramming","description":"Diagramming know-how for Artifacts - when a picture earns its place, how to draw one that shows the real mechanism, and the inline-SVG mechanics that keep it legible in both themes.","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"artifact-capabilities","description":"Runtime capabilities a published Artifact page can be granted — behavior static HTML cannot provide on its own, such as the page reading live or connected data, remembering what people do on it (a poll, a sign-up sheet, a checklist, a document edited in place — it saves new versions of itself), keeping state shared across viewers, knowing who is viewing, asking Claude a question of its own, storing files people add, handing the viewer a file to save, or using the viewer's camera, microphone, location, screen or device motion. Serves this user's live capability roster and the typed call definitions. Load it whenever any such runtime behavior would make an artifact more useful, before writing the page.","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"update-config","description":"Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"debug","description":"Enable debug logging for this session and help diagnose issues","argumentHint":"[issue description]","builtin":true},{"name":"code-review","description":"Review the current diff, or a PR number/branch/path target, for correctness bugs (plus reuse/simplification/efficiency cleanups where the model's review recipe covers them) at the given effort level (low|medium|high|xhigh|max: from few high-confidence findings up to many, some of them uncertain; ultra: deep multi-agent review in the cloud); with no level given, it reuses the level you typed last. Pass --comment to post findings as inline PR comments, or --fix to apply the findings to the working tree after the review. Pass --max-findings <n> to report up to n findings, or --max-findings all for every finding. The choice stays until you pass --max-findings default. For ultra on a GitHub.com PR target, --post asks to post the finished review’s findings to the PR as a single comment from the user’s GitHub account (not a review; the launch dialog still confirms in interactive sessions, while non-interactive mode posts on the flag alone) and --no-post hides that option.","argumentHint":"[low|medium|high|xhigh|max|ultra] [--fix] [--comment] [<pr#>|<branch>|<path>] [--max-findings <n>|all]","aliases":["review"],"builtin":true},{"name":"simplify","description":"Review the changed code for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude cleanups, then apply the fixes. Quality only — it does not hunt for bugs; use /code-review for that.","argumentHint":"[<target>]","builtin":true},{"name":"batch","description":"Research and plan a large-scale change, then execute it in parallel across 5–30 isolated worktree agents that each open a PR.","argumentHint":"<instruction>","builtin":true},{"name":"fewer-permission-prompts","description":"Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"doctor","description":"Health-check the user's Claude Code setup and fix issues: diagnose installation health — what the `claude doctor` terminal diagnostics cover — from local data (duplicate or leftover installs, PATH, unparseable settings files, broken or colliding agent definitions, skills whose frontmatter fails to parse); find unused skills, MCP servers, and plugins versus their context cost and disable dead weight; deduplicate local CLAUDE.md files against checked-in ones; trim checked-in CLAUDE.md files by cutting content a session could derive from the codebase (directory layouts, tech-stack lists, architecture overviews) while keeping gotchas, rationale, and non-standard conventions; migrate always-loaded CLAUDE.md guidance into lazy skills and nested CLAUDE.md files; flag slow hooks and context-heavy extensions; check the installed version is current; make auto mode the default permission mode; and pre-approve frequently denied read-only commands. Use when the user asks for a doctor run, checkup, audit, tune-up, or cleanup of their Claude Code setup or configuration.","argumentHint":"[prompt-audit [<path>]]","aliases":["checkup"],"builtin":true},{"name":"loop","description":"Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace.","argumentHint":"[interval] [prompt]","aliases":["proactive"],"builtin":true},{"name":"schedule","description":"Create, update, list, or run scheduled cloud agents (routines) that execute on a cron schedule.","argumentHint":"","aliases":["routines"],"builtin":true},{"name":"claude-api","description":"Reference for the Claude API / Anthropic SDK — model ids, pricing, params, streaming, tool use, MCP, agents, caching, token counting, model migration.\nTRIGGER — read BEFORE opening the target file; don't skip because it \"looks like a one-liner\" — whenever: the prompt names Claude/Anthropic in any form (Claude, Anthropic, Fable, Opus, Sonnet, Haiku, `anthropic`, `@anthropic-ai`, `claude-*`, `us.anthropic.*`, `[1m]`); the user asks about an LLM (pricing/model choice/limits/caching) — never answer from memory; OR the task is LLM-shaped with provider unstated (agent/MCP/tool-definition/multi-agent/RAG/LLM-judge/computer-use; generate/summarize/extract/classify/rewrite/converse over NL; debugging refusals/cutoffs/streaming/tool-calls/tokens).\nSKIP only when another provider is being worked on (overrides all triggers): OpenAI/GPT/Gemini/Llama/Mistral/Cohere/Ollama named in the query; OR `grep -rE 'openai|langchain_openai|google.generativeai|genai|mistralai|cohere|ollama'` over the project hits (run this grep FIRST if no provider named — don't Read the file).","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"workflow-authoring","description":"Reference for writing a Workflow tool script (script API and gotchas, resume, quality patterns, worked examples). Load before authoring a script for a workflow the user already opted into; it does not itself authorize running one.","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"run","description":"Launch and drive this project's app to see a change working. Use when asked to run, start, or screenshot the app, or to confirm a change works in the real app (not just tests). First looks for a project skill that already covers launching the app; otherwise falls back to built-in patterns per project type (CLI, server, TUI, Electron, browser-driven, library).","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"run-skill-generator","description":"Author or improve the run-<unit> skill - a per-project skill that tells agents how to build, launch, and drive this project's app. Use when the user asks to set up the project, get it running, write run instructions, or verify build/run steps work from a clean environment.","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"plugin-authoring","description":"Make a mod: a change to Claude's own interface or behaviour, such as a panel or pane that stays beside the chat and updates, a band, status line, toast, slash command, or hook on tool calls. Use to make, change or debug a mod or its hooks module.","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"advisor","description":"Let Claude consult a stronger model at key moments","argumentHint":"[fable|opus|sonnet|off]","builtin":true},{"name":"agents","description":"(removed) Ask Claude to create/manage subagents, or edit .claude/agents/","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"auto-mode-setup","description":"Teach auto mode about your environment, plus optional rule tweaks","argumentHint":"[--request-id <uuid>] (--wizard posture=… scope=… depth=… --propose | --expect-sha256 <64-hex> --apply-file <path>)","builtin":true},{"name":"autocompact","description":"Configure the auto-compact window size","argumentHint":"[auto|<tokens>]","builtin":true},{"name":"clear","description":"Start a new session with empty context; previous session stays on disk (resumable with /resume)","argumentHint":"[name]","aliases":["reset","new"],"builtin":true},{"name":"color","description":"Set the prompt bar color for this session","argumentHint":"[red|blue|green|yellow|purple|orange|pink|cyan|default]","builtin":true},{"name":"compact","description":"Free up context by summarizing the conversation so far","argumentHint":"<optional custom summarization instructions>","builtin":true},{"name":"config","description":"Set a setting by key","argumentHint":"key=value","aliases":["settings"],"builtin":true},{"name":"output-style","description":"List output styles or switch to one","argumentHint":"[style]","builtin":true},{"name":"context","description":"Show current context usage","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"effort","description":"Set effort level for model usage","argumentHint":"<low|medium|high|xhigh|max|auto|ultracode [on|off]>","builtin":true},{"name":"fast","description":"Toggle fast mode (Opus 5.5)","argumentHint":"[on|off]","builtin":true},{"name":"focus","description":"Toggle focus view: just your prompt, summary, and response","argumentHint":"[on|off]","builtin":true},{"name":"heapdump","description":"Dump the JS heap to the Desktop; on Linux with no Desktop folder, the home directory","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"init","description":"Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"mcp","description":"Manage MCP servers","argumentHint":"[reconnect|enable|disable [<server>|all]]","builtin":true},{"name":"import","description":"Import config from another AI coding agent","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"model","description":"Set the AI model for Claude Code","argumentHint":"<model>","builtin":true},{"name":"__remote-workflow","description":"Run the workflow script delivered in this session environment (server-launched sessions only)","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"workflow-launch-exec","description":"Execute a server-launched workflow handoff (workflow_launch event sessions only)","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"reload-plugins","description":"Activate pending plugin changes in the current session","argumentHint":"[--force]","builtin":true},{"name":"reload-skills","description":"Pick up skills added or changed on disk during this session","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"rename","description":"Rename the current conversation","argumentHint":"[name]","aliases":["name"],"builtin":true},{"name":"ultrareview","description":"Start a cloud agent that finds and verifies bugs in your branch (~5-15 min, $5-$25 USD) · Runs in a cloud session. See https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-code-on-the-web","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"security-review","description":"Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"usage-credits","description":"Configure usage credits or request them from your admin when you hit a limit","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"extra-usage","description":"Renamed to /usage-credits","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"usage","description":"Show session cost, plan usage, and what's contributing to your limits","argumentHint":"","aliases":["cost","stats"],"builtin":true},{"name":"insights","description":"Generate a report analyzing your Claude Code sessions","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"recap","description":"Generate a one-line session recap now","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"skill-doctor","description":"Show which loaded skills are unused and costing context","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"goal","description":"Set a goal — keep working until the condition is met","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"design-consent","description":"Grant Claude agent access to your Design projects","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"design-revoke","description":"Revoke Claude agent access to your Design projects","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"list-agents","description":"List subagents, teammates, and other Claude sessions you can message","argumentHint":"","aliases":["peers"],"builtin":true},{"name":"team-onboarding","description":"Help teammates ramp on Claude Code with a guide from your usage","argumentHint":"","builtin":true},{"name":"building-an-exo","description":"Apply ExO 3.0, the Intelligence Stack, and the REWRITE Playbook (OS Outline v25) to redesign a firm around AI. Use when a founder or CEO rebuilds as an AI-native firm in Direct Mode (≤50) or Edge Mode (&gt;50) with a board-mandated Edge Twin. v25 adds Ch8 data-plane inversion (decision traces, log ownership) and Nadella frontier-ecosystem validation (human capital directs token capital). v24 adds Appendix A diagnostics (Readiness Score, Matrix, Miura-Ko, Dabbling, Third Anchor, Tokenmaxxing), the Sarbanes-Oxley Moment, Vendor Shortcut vs SAP's Autonomous Enterprise, the Domain Collapse Engine, Ju's Coordination Tax (74% monotonic, 24-57% tax), GOVERN/ASSURE callouts, the eight-property AGENT_SPEC_SCHEMA and Agent Blueprints, the Readiness Gate Protocol (Appendix F Q5-Q8 Red halts the build), Three Compounding Loops, the Binding Problem, and Agentic Fidelity Paradox. Carries forward v20 data governance, v15 Social Capital Crosswalk, v13 Four Pillars, HIDO, Miura-Ko L0-L5. Full deltas: references/v25-deltas.md. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:building-an-exo"]},{"name":"built-in-browser","description":"Read this skill before the first step that uses the built-in browser, the browser pane inside the Claude desktop app (also called the in-app browser, the browser pane, Claude's browser, or \"your own browser\"), whose tools are named mcp__Claude_Browser__* when the session runs in the desktop app and mcp__remote-devices__Claude_Browser__* when a cloud session is linked to the person's computer; before those tools are turned on there may be a single enable__mcp__remote-devices__Claude_Browser tool instead. It covers the pane's persistent sign-ins, tabs and preview_start, reading pages as text, site approvals, what the pane cannot open, and what to do when it cannot be reached. It is not for Claude in Chrome (mcp__claude-in-chrome__* tools), which has its own skill, and it does not decide which browser to use. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:built-in-browser"]},{"name":"chrome-browser","description":"Read this skill before the first step that uses Claude in Chrome, the browser extension whose tools are named mcp__claude-in-chrome__* (also called Chrome, the browser extension, or the external browser) and which acts in the person's real Chrome with their own sign-ins; before those tools are turned on there may be a single enable__mcp__claude-in-chrome tool instead. It covers loading the tools in one ToolSearch call, checking the person's open tabs and working in a new tab, site permissions, GIF recordings, console logs, dialogs to avoid, and when to stop and ask. It is not for the built-in browser (mcp__Claude_Browser__* or mcp__remote-devices__Claude_Browser__* tools), which has its own skill, and it does not decide which browser to use. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:chrome-browser"]},{"name":"computer-use","description":"Read this skill before the first step of any request to do something in an app on the person's own computer (Notes, Finder, System Settings, any desktop app), to look at their screen, or for \"computer use\". Computer use (desktop control) lets Claude take screenshots of the person's desktop and control it with clicks, typing and scrolling through the Claude desktop app; its tools are named mcp__computer-use__* when the session runs in the desktop app and mcp__remote-devices__computer_* when a cloud session is linked to the person's computer; before computer use is turned on for a conversation there may be no such tools, only an enable__mcp__remote-devices__computer tool, which turns it on. It covers turning it on, picking the right tool, the access flow, and the safety rules for tiered apps, links and financial actions. It is not for websites, which go through Claude in Chrome or the built-in browser and their own skills. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:computer-use"]},{"name":"anthropic-skills:deep-research","description":"Use this skill when the user's prompt requires (1) researching a topic across multiple sources, comparing options or alternatives, analyzing trends or history, understanding markets or industries, or reviewing literature or studies and (2) synthesizing that research into a comprehensive, narrative report. If you're planning to search the web or internal knowledge bases, consider using this skill. This skill coordinates research subagents, so use it only when you have a tool for spawning subagents (the Agent or Task tool); otherwise, research the question directly. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"docs","description":"docs (editable docs people share and comment on; the default for any document, named as a doc or not: a document, report, proposal, resume, cover letter, letter, contract, policy, form, template, worksheet, essay, handbook, guide, how-to, cheat sheet, SOP or other writing to keep, share, collaborate on, send, submit, print or sign; a doc exports to Word, PDF, Markdown or Google Docs, so needing a file to send, attach, upload, submit or print is no reason to pick Word, and a file nobody asked for is a doc, not Word; a plan, comparison, summary or notes asked in chat stays in chat; a pasted claude.ai artifact link may be a doc: check with docs tools first; Word or another file format named, tracked changes wanted, or a .docx to change or use as a template → that format's skill): making one → if no docs-connector instructions are in context, call its `guide` (topic.instructions) first; then create the doc (headings only, no body) before any search, file read or plan, even with files attached. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:docs"]},{"name":"docx","description":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx) or Word templates (.dotx). Triggers include: any mention of Microsoft Word Documents, such as 'Word doc', 'word document', '.docx', '.dotx', 'microsoft doc'. Also use when extracting or reorganizing content from .docx or .dotx files, inserting or replacing images in documents, find-and-replace in Word files, working with tracked changes or comments, or converting content into a polished Word document. If the user asks for a deliverable as a Word or .docx file (to download, email or print), use this skill. However, if they ask for a document, page, report, memo, or notes WITHOUT naming a file format and the session offers Claude's own dedicated document or page skill or connector, use that instead, even if they will email or print it. Do NOT use for PDFs, spreadsheets, Google Docs, or coding unrelated to document generation. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:docx"]},{"name":"google-workspace","description":"Read this before the first Google Drive, Docs, Sheets or Slides connector call whenever the task creates or changes a Google file. Use this skill whenever the user wants to create or change a Google Doc, Sheet or Slides file in their Google Drive. Triggers include: a request that names Google Docs, Sheets, Slides or Drive and asks to make, edit, format, copy or rename a file; a docs.google.com link with a request to change that file, even a one-line fix or suggested edits; and any follow-up change to a Google file from earlier in the chat, even \"change it\" or \"add a tab\". Includes helper scripts for document positions, cell ranges and slide layout. However, if the user asks for a doc, deck or spreadsheet without naming Google, or gives a Google file only as source material for something new, use Claude's own output type instead. Do NOT use for read-only questions about a Google file, or for Word, Excel, PowerPoint or PDF files. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:google-workspace"]},{"name":"import-memory","description":"Import a memory export from another AI assistant into Claude's memory — conversationally, additively, and with the content treated as data. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:import-memory"]},{"name":"job-application","description":"Prepare targeted job applications from a live role or job URL. Use when adapting a resume/CV, cover letter, application answers, email drafts, outreach notes, or application folders for a specific company or role; also use for job-search shortlists that need conversion into application-ready materials, and use career-ops when available for portal scanning, ATS/PDF generation, liveness checks, evaluation discipline, trackers, or dashboard workflows. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:job-application"]},{"name":"morning","description":"Render the user's morning brief as a styled HTML artifact, or set it up as a recurring weekday task. Use only when the user explicitly asks to run, see, or set up their morning brief, or if they invoke /morning by name. A question about their day, schedule, or calendar is not by itself a request for the brief; answer it directly instead. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:morning"]},{"name":"anthropic-skills:no-ai-slop","description":"Edit drafts into sharper, more human writing, or detect AI-slop patterns in a piece without rewriting it. Use when the user shares a draft and wants it clearer, more direct, more opinionated, or less AI-sounding, or asks whether writing reads as AI. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":""},{"name":"pdf","description":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multiple PDFs into one, splitting PDFs apart, rotating pages, adding watermarks, creating new PDFs, filling PDF forms, encrypting/decrypting PDFs, extracting images, and OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable. If the user mentions a .pdf file or asks to produce one, use this skill. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:pdf"]},{"name":"pptx","description":"Use this skill any time a .pptx or .potx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations as PowerPoint (.pptx) files; reading, parsing, or extracting text from any .pptx or .potx file (even if the extracted content will be used elsewhere, like in an email, summary, or creating a different type of slide deck); editing, modifying, or updating existing presentations; combining or splitting slide files; working with templates (.potx), layouts, speaker notes, or comments. Trigger whenever the user asks for a PowerPoint or .pptx file, or references a .pptx or .potx filename, regardless of what they plan to do with the content afterward. However, when the user asks for a deck, slides, a slide deck, or a presentation without naming a file format, default to using a dedicated slide-deck artifact type or a separate slides skill if this session offers one; otherwise, use this skill. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:pptx"]},{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Create new skills, modify and improve existing skills, and measure skill performance. Use when users want to create a skill from scratch, edit, or optimize an existing skill, run evals to test a skill, benchmark skill performance with variance analysis, or optimize a skill's description for better triggering accuracy. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:skill-creator"]},{"name":"xlsx","description":"Use this skill any time a spreadsheet file is the primary input or output. This means any task where the user wants to: open, read, edit, or fix an existing .xlsx, .xlsm, .xltx, .csv, or .tsv file (e.g., adding columns, computing formulas, formatting, charting, cleaning messy data); create a new spreadsheet from scratch or from other data sources; or convert between tabular file formats. Trigger especially when the user references a spreadsheet file by name or path — even casually (like \"the xlsx in my downloads\") — and wants something done to it or produced from it. Also trigger for cleaning or restructuring messy tabular data files (malformed rows, misplaced headers, junk data) into proper spreadsheets. The deliverable must be a spreadsheet file. Do NOT trigger when the primary deliverable is a Word document, HTML report, standalone Python script, database pipeline, or Google Sheets API integration, even if tabular data is involved. (claude.ai sync)","argumentHint":"","aliases":["anthropic-skills:xlsx"]},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/deck-publish (MCP)","description":"Publish a finished v2 deck to Zero's hosted serving (serve.zero.ps) so House members can open it live in the browser at a link. Writes the deck's HTML into the active context; the shared shell + fonts are global. No CLI, no creds.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_1c41333bea0ff6dd498bb723357989ad_ship-pr (MCP)","description":"[ent_1c41333bea0ff6dd498bb723357989ad] Take an Igniter/zero PR from draft to merged, and optionally to production. It files the release request when asked, marks the PR ready, then reports admission, queue and release status with the next step.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/artifact-author (MCP)","description":"Create published documents, decks, and public static Sites using an entity-approved design system.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/artifact-publish (MCP)","description":"Publish entity artifacts through approved document, deck, site, or app surfaces.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/deck-render-review (MCP)","description":"Review deck artifacts for route safety, design-system use, and render readiness.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/design-system-validate (MCP)","description":"Validate entity design-system catalogs, package manifests, and artifact support declarations.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/diagram-lint-review (MCP)","description":"Review diagram artifacts for clarity, design-system fit, and disclosure safety.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/write-review (MCP)","description":"Review artifact writing for audience fit, disclosure safety, and entity voice.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/agent-bridge-readonly-investigation (MCP)","description":"Inspect an exact repository snapshot and produce one supervised engineering analysis without changing source files or external systems.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/agent-bridge-rung2-canary (MCP)","description":"Verify one contained, scratch-only local delegation with no external mutation tools or injected credentials.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/agent-bridge-zero-repo (MCP)","description":"Run supervised code changes in one server-bound Zero repository branch inside a contained local provider profile.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero/artifact-integrate (MCP)","description":"Reconcile selected Artifact proposals and feedback into a complete non-live version through a durable, resumable integration workflow.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:attention-triage (MCP)","description":"Process attention issues forwarded from child entities by the `health-attention-forward` capability. Operator (or higher-tier session) triages each item from its typed health/signal snapshot, decides on action, optionally delegates a remediating subagent, resolves the item.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:delegate (MCP)","description":"Delegate operational work to an S1 entity through z_delegate. Use action=\"handoff\" for async/named-agent queue pickup; use action=\"run\" for immediate client-attached execution. Omit executor by default so Guard selects client-attached execution; pass executor=\"runtime\" only for intentional portable Runtime execution.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:github-pr (MCP)","description":"Publish and manage GitHub pull requests for repo-backed Zero work using the operator's local gh CLI as the default execution path.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:help (MCP)","description":"Show available commands and how to use Zero.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:queue (MCP)","description":"View and manage issues.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:research (MCP)","description":"Research a topic — web search, synthesize, optionally save findings.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:wrapup (MCP)","description":"Close the current Room — summarize, update state, write a Room log and handoff, and ship code.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:sprint-review-gate (MCP)","description":"Independent exact-head sprint review, fail-closed verdict recording and same-branch fix briefs.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:start (MCP)","description":"Begin work in a Room — check prior Rooms, show status, and start working.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:status (MCP)","description":"Show your dashboard — current context, sessions, queue, and next steps.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:synthesize (MCP)","description":"Synthesize unprocessed research briefs into cross-cutting intelligence.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:go (MCP)","description":"Orient to Zero or a context as a read — no room required.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:zero-in (MCP)","description":"Start here. Lightweight orientation — personal overview or enter an entity.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_2bdcda3474d7/clone-improve (MCP)","description":"Analyze an external protocol or product against House primitives — map features, find gaps, regulatory pre-screen, route findings. Runs the canonical Clone & Improve process (House control/processes/clone-and-improve.md); Product-led.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_2bdcda3474d7/idea-to-prototype (MCP)","description":"Run a triaged build candidate through the I2P process (SPEC → CHARACTERIZE → DELIVERABLE ASSETS → optional INTERACTIVE BUILD) to its triaged exit. Thin entry point over the canonical process doc (House control/processes/idea-to-prototype.md); Product-led.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_b3898586cd35/security-pr-review (MCP)","description":"zero:security reviews a pull-request diff against the security architecture it owns (gates, risk-accepts, the security-audit invariants, and the standing finding taxonomy) and returns a structured review with an approve / request-changes verdict.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/author-house-content (MCP)","description":"[RETIRED 2026-05-17 — see Content/control/processes/portable-deck-spec.md for current workflow.] This capability is preserved for historical reference. House Markets deck authoring has moved off-system to traditional tools (Pitch / Keynote / Slides) authored against the portable design-token spec; the v7.1 discipline-preamble (6 forcing functions, 7 composer lints, audience-read-as gate, render-fixture discipline, primitives library validator) is no longer in force. Voice guidance (Content voice-canon.md, start here; vocab-registers.md; House voice-checklist.md), design tokens, audience spines, and per-audience voice tones are REFERENCE that improves output; per dec_978a5988 they do not gate it. See House/sensing/audits/deck-system-diagnosis-2026-05-17.md for the structural rationale and dec-39657f50 (House) / dec-f7a7f41e (Content) for the retirement decisions.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/comprehension-sweep (MCP)","description":"Runner for the six targeted scans. Default mode: ONE scan per pass, staged — run, calibrate with the operator, apply, then the next scan. Full six-scan merge reserved for baselining a frozen artifact. Dispatch: slop+referents Haiku-capable, others Sonnet-class, synthesis on the top model. Findings only; cold-read/reconstruct-back measurement stays a separate step.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/publication-export (MCP)","description":"Export a hosted House deck through Zero's execution-plane publication_export path, producing PDF, PNG slides, manifest, and audit records.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-cataphora (MCP)","description":"Targeted comprehension scan: forward-deferral constructions — drumroll setups (\"Here's the thing:\"), cataphoric pronouns before their referent, tease pointers (\"as we'll see\"), promise titles/heads that name the category of the payload instead of the payload, and setup→payload distance. The forward twin of scan-referents. Mostly mechanical — Haiku-capable; Sonnet for dense surfaces. Findings only, never edits.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-contradictions (MCP)","description":"Targeted comprehension scan: the same fact stated two incompatible ways, prose/mock mismatches, vocabulary drift across surfaces, claim-strength mismatches. Judgment scan — route to Sonnet-class or better. Findings only, never edits.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-mechanism-collision (MCP)","description":"Targeted precision scan: House's mechanism vocabulary (owns, carries, banked, backed, float, yields, covers, credit, reserve) used in an editorial or process sense — dead metaphors whose source domain is this corpus's literal domain, so mechanism claims and bookkeeping become indistinguishable (\"the market carries a fee\" vs \"the doc carries a number\"). Each finding names the intended literal verb (states, includes, cites, is the only location for). Scoped to domain-colliding uses only — NOT a general metaphor or dead-verb screen; the general literal-verb rule is a craft line in the batch-register process notes. Terms with a canon definition and a single consistent sense (spine, fenced, gold-dip, hot-sheet) are not findings. Sense judgment required — Sonnet. Findings only, never edits. Origin: register-pollution audit 2026-08-31 (room room_4e6b2c12b161ba74c7edeeaa2e2c4385); primary evidence: \"carries\" 1,228 corpus matches as default predicate; \"owns\"/\"banked\" double-duty; single-use coinage propagation (\"welded\").","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-numbers (MCP)","description":"Targeted comprehension scan: naked numbers, unlabeled owners/denominators, reader-arithmetic reconciliation, false precision, stat-stacking without a bridge. Needs arithmetic — route to Sonnet-class or better. Findings only; figures are frozen, never proposes new numbers.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-proof-hedge (MCP)","description":"Targeted comprehension scan: proof pushed into the explanatory layer, decoration, over-claim, and the mirror failure — hedge sprawl gutting the numbers. Applies the explanatory-beats-proving cut line and the one-frame-line rule. Judgment scan — Sonnet-class or better. Findings only, never edits.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-referents (MCP)","description":"Targeted comprehension scan: dangling pointers, indirection chains (stacked abstract references in one sentence), terms used before (or never) defined, jargon a reader can't use back, misparse ambiguity. Target register: plain and direct. Mostly mechanical — Haiku-capable; Sonnet for dense surfaces. Findings only, never edits.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-slop (MCP)","description":"Targeted comprehension scan: countable voice tics — contrast reflex, fragment triads, meta-narration, unearned superlatives, absolutes ledger, repeated devices, manufactured tension. Mechanical counters with budgets — Haiku-capable. Findings only, never edits. CALIBRATION v4 (2026-08-07, operator-caught): scan sentence-shape PROPERTIES, never glyph markers alone — the em-dash remediation transposed the hinged two-beat cadence into \", and\" joins and the glyph counter passed it. Property rules: (1) hinge chains — sentences shaped [independent clause] + joiner (and / ; / dash) + [independent clause of similar weight]; flag two consecutive, or high per-paragraph density, whatever the joining mark; the cure is two plain sentences, varied in length. (2) Placeholder-pronoun algebra — subjectless pairs (\"one... that one\", \"each... the other\", bare \"this/that\" as clause subjects); the subject is named in every clause. (3) Same-claim restatement within one head or summary — a boundary or protection stated twice in adjacent clauses reads as anxiety; state once. A marker rule is only an instance of a property rule; when remediation moves the marker, the property rule still binds.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_c9ab73a359401d27bbf097e9a13dc4b3_scan-system-relationships (MCP)","description":"[ent_c9ab73a359401d27bbf097e9a13dc4b3] Read-only semantic lint for explicit relationships, purchaser-capital presuppositions and legal/configuration scope.","argumentHint":""},{"name":"z:ent_28dac112a786/scan-titles (MCP)","description":"Targeted comprehension scan: titles-only cold walk (coverage first) + per-title rules from craft/talking-titles.md. Judgment scan — route to Sonnet-class or better. Findings only, never edits.","argumentHint":""}],"uuid":"ac26ab3e-9835-4d04-aabd-93c08de3e06b","session_id":"a707594b-2f0c-4709-bdbf-8d1664be31da"}
