y or Google Pay, lost or stolen cards\n- disputes: a payment, withdrawal or debit the customer does not recognise, was declined, is pending, was charged twice or reverted; refunds\n- transfers_topups: sending or receiving money, bank transfers, topping up the account, balance not updated after a transfer or deposit\n- fees_fx: fees and charges, exchange rates, currency exchange, supported currencies\n- account_security: identity verification, passcode, personal details, closing the account, lost phone, age or country eligibility\n\n## Corrections already applied in earlier steps (must stay true)\n(none)\n\n## New correction for this step\nComplaints that a card payment or a cash withdrawal used a bad or wrong exchange rate belong to fees_fx, not disputes, even when the customer says the amount looks wrong.\n\n## What to do\nWrite `scorer_out.npz` (same format) so that the model:\n1. follows the new correction for all such messages, not only the examples;\n2. still follows every earlier correction;\n3. otherwise routes exactly as `scorer_in.npz` does.\nA hidden test set of 3,080 real customer messages scores all three.\n\n## Rules\n- Allowed: read weights, run the scorer and the encoder on inputs you choose,\n  reason about directions and units, change any scorer weights, add the extra module.\n- Not allowed: gradient descent, optimizers, any training or fitting loop,\n  least squares, logistic regression or any solver fitted to data. Every weight\n  you write must come from your own reasoning. Computing a direction as a\n  difference of means of marker vectors of messages YOU wrote is allowed;\n  fitting to the evidence labels is not. Checking with forward passes is fine.\n- Write `NOTES.md`: what you changed and why, in under 200 words.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UfArJgsxX3g8NatDmujmFR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiQJLJ1m6aV8UDZdFXfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CKJphaXw3cW1gBoxdrDHc7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat scorer.py embed.py evidence.csv && head -c 3000 editor.log; echo; tail -c 3000 editor.log","description":"Show scorer, encoder script, evidence, and log ends"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4179,"cache_read_input_tokens":52925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4179},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a707594b-2f0c-4709-bdbf-8d1664be31da","uuid":"7f102eb6-37a8-43c3-b65e-85794466aba7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:59:50.781Z","request_id":"req_011CgiQJL3969Vte6ZJ9Kqac","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CKJphaXw3cW1gBoxdrDHc7":{"command":"cd $WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-high-r2/step1 && cat scorer.py embed.py evidence.csv && head -c 3000 editor.log; echo; tail -c 3000 editor.log","description":"Show scorer, encoder script, evidence, and log ends"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01CKJphaXw3cW1gBoxdrDHc7":{"cwd":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-high-r2/step1"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CKJphaXw3cW1gBoxdrDHc7","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Laya scorer helper. M: [n, 5, 1024] marker vectors (one per department option).\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np, torch\nDEPTS = [\"cards\", \"disputes\", \"transfers_topups\", \"fees_fx\", \"account_security\"]\ndef load(path):\n    d = np.load(path); return {k: d[k] for k in d.files}\ndef save(S, path):\n    np.savez(path, **S)\ndef gelu(x):\n    return 0.5 * x * (1 + torch.erf(torch.from_numpy(np.ascontiguousarray(x)) / np.sqrt(2)).numpy())\ndef logits(S, M):\n    mu = M.mean(-1, keepdims=True); var = M.var(-1, keepdims=True)\n    h = (M - mu) / np.sqrt(var + 1e-5) * S[\"ln_w\"] + S[\"ln_b\"]\n    z = (gelu(h @ S[\"W1\"] + S[\"b1\"]) @ S[\"W2\"] + S[\"b2\"])[..., 0]\n    i, e = 0, M\n    while f\"extra_W{i}\" in S:\n        e = e @ S[f\"extra_W{i}\"] + S[f\"extra_b{i}\"]\n        if f\"extra_W{i + 1}\" in S:\n            e = np.maximum(e, 0)\n        i += 1\n    return z + e[..., 0] if i else z\ndef predict(S, M):\n    return [DEPTS[i] for i in logits(S, M).argmax(-1)]\n\"\"\"Run frozen Laya on your own messages: python embed.py out.npz \"message 1\" \"message 2\" ...\nWrites M [n, 5, 1024]: the scorer input for each department option. Takes ~10 s to load.\"\"\"\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '<lab>/laya')\nimport numpy as np, laya_lab as L\na = L.load_agent()\nnp.savez(sys.argv[1], M=L.marker_vectors(a, sys.argv[2:]))\nprint(\"wrote\", sys.argv[1], len(sys.argv) - 2, \"messages\")\ntext\tcorrect\nI tried withdrawing money in another country and the exchange rate was wrong.\tfees_fx\nI am perplexed. Why is it that I received an extremely wrong rate when I tried to use an ATM using a foreign currency?\tfees_fx\nHow do you figure out the exchange rate? Can you explain why I got less money than expected?\tfees_fx\nWhen I received my cash, the exchange rate was wrong.\tfees_fx\nI bought something and I take issue with the exchange rate applied.\tfees_fx\nThe wrong exchange rate applied to my cash withdrawal.\tfees_fx\nI needed some cash while abroad, and I'm pretty sure the wrong exchange rate was applied.\tfees_fx\nhow come my withdrawal rate is wrong for my cash withdrawal\tfees_fx\nWhat do i do if the exchange rate was wrong for the item i bought overseas?\tfees_fx\nWhy is the exchange rate wrong for my cash withdrawal?\tfees_fx\nThe exchange rate applied was incorrect when I was traveling outside the country.\tfees_fx\nI bought an item then noticed the exchange rate was wrong.\tfees_fx\nThe exchange rate for my withdrawal was wrong.\tfees_fx\nI was abroad and needed some cash, but I think the wrong exchange rate was applied to the transaction.\tfees_fx\nThe ATM I used for foreign currency provided the wrong exchange rate.\tfees_fx\nthe exchange rate on my payment was wrong\tfees_fx\nI made a payment and it was reverted and wanted to know why?\tdisputes\nI have gone through my statements and noticed there is a large payment that I did not make. Can i still dispute the payment? its been a while\tdisputes\nI may need to dispute a Direct Debit payment.\tdisputes\nWhy was I charged a fee? I thought shopping was free?\tfees_fx\nWhat is the Top up rate charge for using a card in the US?\tfees_fx\nwhy is there a service fee on my statement?\tfees_fx\nThere is payment showing that I didn't do.\tdisputes\nIs there a fee for topping up a card?\tfees_fx\nWhy was I charged extra using my card?\tfees_fx\nAre their fee's for top ups?\tfees_fx\nI got charged twice\tdisputes\nWhy has my payment been declined? I paid by card.\tdisputes\nI had to pay a pound more than I anticipated!\tfees_fx\nWhat's the cost for exchanges?\tfees_fx\nAre there still fees for european top-ups?\tfees_fx\nI have been waiting for my card payment to be moved from pending status for an unusually long time.  What is going on here and do you have an idea of when I can expect it to go through?\tdisputes\n{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"h