{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiSg8N1trHbQBH88LNek","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F6n8Fe5GdxNmNWyDvKhpYD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-high-r2/step1/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 1: wrong exchange rate -> fees_fx\n\n**Original scorer weights are unchanged.** I added only an extra ReLU module (5 layers) that adds up to +5 to the fees_fx logit. It outputs exactly 0 everywhere else.\n\n**Why a module.** Each marker vector is about 99% a fixed curve of its own logit. Topic information sits in small directions, about 1000x smaller in scale. Mean differences found these only after I divided each principal axis (from all my messages, without labels) by its standard deviation.\n\n**Detectors** (fees_fx option, 192 axes): the mean of my ~600 wrong-rate complaints against (a) all other options and messages, (b) plain FX questions, (c) dispute near-misses (\"charged twice\", wrong amount). Each is scaled so 0 = halfway between the means. The module fires only when all three are > 0: min built with ReLUs, then a steep ramp capped at +5.\n\n**Scale-free in raw space.** A sum-zero weight gives std(x)·(w·z). The bias rides on a \"flat\" mean vector, which has its 256 varying axes removed.\n\n**Checks** (held-out, my own and evidence): 54/58 targets move to fees_fx; 186/187 others keep their route. Evidence: 31/32 (one target missed). No other option's logit ever changes.\n\n**Not used:** evidence labels, training or solvers.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1845,"cache_read_input_tokens":227883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1845},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null}