{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiShn2TFY2hBf9QvrJms","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gb1dZ5DsqF7tAXhCT9Unr6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-claude-502-<proj>/memory/laya-marker-vector-geometry.md","content":"---\nname: laya-marker-vector-geometry\ndescription: Laya weight-edit lab: marker vectors are ~a curve of their own logit; topic needs unit-variance PCA directions; raw-space scale pitfall\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nLaya weight-edit lab (3 steps, step 1 done 2026-11-04: wrong exchange rate -> fees_fx).\n\n- Each option's marker vector is ~99% a 1-D curve of its own logit (PC0 corr 1.00 with logit, PC1 = curve bend). Topic info lives in axes ~1000x smaller.\n- Plain mean differences fail. Mean difference after dividing each PCA axis (label-free, my own messages) by its std works: held-out AUC ~0.97-0.98 at K=192-256 axes.\n- Need several hundred template messages of my own; ~50 is too noisy.\n- Raw-space ReLU unit: sum-zero weights give std(x)*(w.z). Carry the bias on mu with its top-256 PCs removed. Using plain mu made the unit fire on other options (big bug).\n- Working design: AND (min via ReLUs) of 3 detectors on the target option, then a ramp capped at +5. Output is exactly 0 elsewhere, so other routes stay bitwise identical.\n- Scripts live in the step-1 session scratchpad (laya_build2.py, laya_eval.py, laya_leakcheck.py).\n\n**Why:** steps 2-3 add corrections on top of this and must keep step 1 true.\n**How to apply:** start from scorer_out.npz of step 1, add a new detector group in parallel (sum outputs), and run a leak check so no direction message equals an evidence message. See [[laya-step1-result]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1231,"cache_read_input_tokens":230851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1231},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a707594b-2f0c-4709-bdbf-8d1664be31da","uuid":"8221130d-aa75-427d-bfcd-55fd51898336","timestamp":"2026-11-04T19:31:28.483Z","request_id":"req_011CgiShmmpDNvM8xrnwXqv8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Gb1dZ5DsqF7tAXhCT9Unr6":{"file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-claude-502-<proj>/memory/laya-marker-vector-geometry.md","content":"---\nname: laya-marker-vector-geometry\ndescription: Laya weight-edit lab: marker vectors are ~a curve of their own logit; topic needs unit-variance PCA directions; raw-space scale pitfall\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nLaya weight-edit lab (3 steps, step 1 done 2026-11-04: wrong exchange rate -> fees_fx).\n\n- Each option's marker vector is ~99% a 1-D curve of its own logit (PC0 corr 1.00 with logit, PC1 = curve bend). Topic info lives in axes ~1000x smaller.\n- Plain mean differences fail. Mean difference after dividing each PCA axis (label-free, my own messages) by its std works: held-out AUC ~0.97-0.98 at K=192-256 axes.\n- Need several hundred template messages of my own; ~50 is too noisy.\n- Raw-space ReLU unit: sum-zero weights give std(x)*(w.z). Carry the bias on mu with its top-256 PCs removed. Using plain mu made the unit fire on other options (big bug).\n- Working design: AND (min via ReLUs) of 3 detectors on the target option, then a ramp capped at +5. Output is exactly 0 elsewhere, so other routes stay bitwise identical.\n- Scripts live in the step-1 session scratchpad (laya_build2.py, laya_eval.py, laya_leakcheck.py).\n\n**Why:** steps 2-3 add corrections on top of this and must keep step 1 true.\n**How to apply:** start from scorer_out.npz of step 1, add a new detector group in parallel (sum outputs), and run a leak check so no direction message equals an evidence message. See [[laya-step1-result]].\n"}}}
